# Handlers

You clicked a button and want this card to update. Counter does that with
a fragment that morphs `#counter`:

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/counter/increment")>
    Increment
</button>
```

```rocci
@post:fragment("/actions/counter/increment") = |{ db }| {
    count = increment_count!(db)?
    counterCard({ count: count })
}
```

`@post("/path")` is a Rocci action (Roc string, double quotes). A quoted
`"@post('…')"` is opaque Datastar JS. For row-specific URLs, make the
attribute a Roc expression.

Spell every route as `@method:role(path)`.

## Choose a shape

| Goal | Declaration | Browser result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Full page | `@get:view("path")` | Document load or navigate |
| Read an HTML fragment | `@get:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Replace HTML after a mutation | `@post:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Perform a write, no representation | `@post:command("path")` | Empty SSE to Datastar; 204 otherwise |
| Stream shared HTML | `@get:live("path")` | Long-lived SSE at that path |

There is no default method. Mutation fragments and commands also allow
`@put`, `@patch`, and `@delete`. Live paths are plural; use one coherence
stream when possible. Do not morph the same `id` from both a finite
fragment and a live stream.

Commands return `{}` and carry no success representation.

One-shot: [Counter](/examples/counter/).
Shared stream: [Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).
The full matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Request, errors, logging

Generated dispatch calls `handler!(context, request)`. List `request`
when you read the body, headers, or route data. Keep `?` at the effectful
edge. A failing handler returns HTTP 500. `rocci run --log-handlers`
prints the matched route. Log with `Stderr.line!` from handlers, never
from `@component`.

Exact forms: [Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/),
[Server](/docs/reference/language/server/).

Next: [Custom applications](/docs/applications/custom/).
